<%- include('partials/header') %>

<header class="page-intro">
  <p class="eyebrow">Your information</p>

  <h1>Privacy & Data Protection</h1>

  <p class="page-intro__text">
    This page explains how information submitted through the
    Aquarium World Contact form is handled.
  </p>
</header>

<section class="content-panel">

  <h2>About this website</h2>
  <p>
    Aquarium World is a fictional website developed as part of the
    QHO431 Web Technologies academic assessment. For the purposes of
    this demonstration website, Aquarium World is treated as the data
    controller for information submitted through the Contact form.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    When you use the Contact form, the website collects your name,
    email address and message. Only information necessary to respond
    to your enquiry is requested.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use this information</h2>
  <p>
    The information is used only to receive, review and respond to
    enquiries submitted through the Contact form. It is not used for
    marketing or automated decision-making.
  </p>

  <h2>Lawful basis</h2>
  <p>
    The processing is based on legitimate interests: responding to
    enquiries that users choose to submit. This use is limited to what
    a user would reasonably expect when contacting the aquarium.
  </p>

  <h2>How the information is stored</h2>
  <p>
    Contact submissions are stored in the website's SQLite database.
    Input is validated on the server and database queries use
    parameterised placeholders to reduce security risks.
  </p>

  <h2>How long information is kept</h2>
  <p>
    Contact information should be retained only for as long as
    necessary to respond to and resolve the enquiry, and should then
    be deleted when it is no longer required.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing of information</h2>
  <p>
    The demonstration website does not use submitted Contact
    information for marketing and does not implement sharing of this
    information with third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>Your data rights</h2>
  <p>
    UK data-protection law gives individuals rights relating to their
    personal information. These may include rights to access,
    correction, erasure or restriction depending on the circumstances.
    Individuals may also raise concerns with the Information
    Commissioner's Office (ICO).
  </p>

  <h2>Academic project notice</h2>
  <p>
    This website is an academic demonstration and does not represent
    a real operating aquarium business. No Data Protection Officer has
    been appointed for this project.
  </p>

</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>